(A Brief History of Cryptography) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 12 Tf
50 780 Td
(Cryptography - the art of creating and breaking codes - dates back millennia.) Tj
ET
BT
50 760 Td
(One of the earliest known ciphers is the Caesar cipher, used by Julius Caesar) Tj
ET
BT
50 740 Td
(around 58 BC to protect military communications.) Tj
ET
BT
50 710 Td
(The Middle Ages brought more sophisticated ciphers, such as the Vigenere cipher,) Tj
ET
BT
50 695 Td
(which used a keyword to create polyalphabetic substitution.) Tj
ET
BT
50 665 Td
(The 20th century revolutionized cryptography with the Enigma machine,) Tj
ET
BT
50 650 Td
(developed in Germany in the 1920s and used extensively during World War II.) Tj
ET
BT
50 635 Td
(Alan Turing's work at Bletchley Park was crucial in breaking Enigma) Tj
ET
BT
50 620 Td
(and contributed significantly to the Allied victory.) Tj
ET
BT
50 590 Td
(The modern era began with public-key cryptography in the 1970s.) Tj
ET
BT
50 575 Td
(RSA (Rivest-Shamir-Adleman) became the first practical public-key) Tj
ET
BT
50 560 Td
(cryptosystem.) Tj
ET
BT
50 530 Td
(Today, cryptography secures everything from online banking to messengers.) Tj
ET
BT
50 510 Td
(However, even modern systems have hidden vulnerabilities that require) Tj
ET
BT
50 495 Td
(deep understanding of cryptographic principles and implementation details.) Tj
ET
BT
50 460 Td
(The study of cryptography is essential for anyone working in cybersecurity.) Tj
ET
BT
50 435 Td
(It combines mathematics, computer science, and creative thinking.) Tj
ET
BT
50 405 Td
(This document contains hidden information that requires technical analysis) Tj
ET
BT
50 390 Td
(to uncover. Can you find what lies beneath the surface?) Tj
ET
BT
50 360 Td
